### Auto Width (Large Dataset)

For datasets with many data points (e.g. 31 daily candles), use `barWidth: "auto"` to make candles fluid with a fixed minimum gap:

```tsx
<CandleStickChart
  data={dailyData} // 31 data points
  candleStickGroupConfig={{
    barWidth: "auto",
    xAxis: true,
    xAxisConfig: { tickCount: 8 },
    hoverBadge: true,
  }}
/>
```

XAxis tick labels are automatically thinned to prevent overlap on narrow viewports — the group measures the container width and widest label, then caps the visible tick count while always keeping the first and last ticks. High/low dots also scale down automatically when candles become narrower than the dot size.

For long category labels, use `xAxisConfig.maxLines` and `xAxisConfig.labelWidth` to enable multiline wrapping:

```tsx
<CandleStickChart
  data={longLabelData}
  candleStickGroupConfig={{
    xAxis: true,
    xAxisConfig: {
      maxLines: 2,
      labelWidth: 80,
    },
  }}
/>
```

See [CandleStickGroup.md](./CandleStickGroup.md) for full auto width mode details and [CandleStick.md](./CandleStick.md) for dot size capping.

## Legend Auto-Generation

When `chartLegend={true}`, legend items are resolved in priority order:

1. **Manual items**: `chartLegendConfig.items` (highest priority)
2. **Single label**: `chartLegendConfig.categoryLabelValue` creates a one-item legend
3. **Auto from data**: Uses the first data point's category as the label with its color (if provided)

## Height Behavior

The chart uses a fixed-height flex column layout:

- `ChartHeader`, `ChartLegend`, `DataDisplay`, and `ChartFooter` take their natural height
- `CandleStickGroup` is wrapped in a `flex: 1; minHeight: 0` container that fills the remaining space
- `CandleStickGroup` receives `height="100%"` to fill the wrapper

This means the group automatically adjusts when optional sections are toggled on/off.

## DataDisplay Hover Integration

When `dataDisplayConfig.mode === "hover"`:

1. Hovering a candle updates `DataDisplay` values dynamically:
   - `mainLabelValue` shows the hovered category label
   - `dataHead.dataLeadValue` shows the close value (formatted)
   - `dataBadgeSemanticConfig.dataBadgeSemanticValue` shows percentage of total
2. Custom formatters (`formatHoverLeadValue`, `formatHoverBadgeValue`) allow full control
3. The group's `onBarHover` callback still fires for external consumers
4. The stable `dataDisplayId` from `useChartAccessibility` links candles to the DataDisplay via `aria-controls`

## Entry Animation

When `animated={true}`, each candle scales up from its **vertical center** with staggered fade-in. The animation uses `enterAnimation` design tokens resolved via `useEntryAnimation` -- no hardcoded values.

- **Collapsed state**: candle is at its real position but `transform: scaleY(0)` collapses it to a line at center (`transformOrigin: center`)
- **Expanded state**: `transform: scaleY(1)` -- full size at the same position
- **Transitioned properties**: `transform`, `opacity` with per-candle stagger via `offsetDelay`
- **Settlement**: after all entry transitions complete, subsequent data changes use `useDataTransition` timing

See [CandleStickGroup.md](./CandleStickGroup.md) for full animation details and token reference.

## Data Transition

When `animated={true}` and data changes after initial entry animation settles:

- **Same count** (e.g. 7 → 7 candles): body heights, wick heights, and vertical positions smoothly transition using `transitionAnimation` tokens. No stagger, no fade.
- **Different count** (e.g. 7 → 10 candles): current candles cross-fade out, new candles cross-fade in. No stagger delay.

The group manages a `displayData` state, a `displayBarWidth` state, and a `crossFadePhase` state machine (`"stable"` → `"out"` → `"in"` → `"stable"`). Inner element transitions (`height` on body/wicks) are passed via `innerTransition` to each `CandleStick`.

When a data transition also changes the `barWidth` (e.g. switching from a fixed-width dataset to an auto-width dataset), the group freezes the outgoing layout mode during the "out" phase via `displayBarWidth`. This prevents old candles from flashing at the new layout before fading out.

See [CandleStickGroup.md](./CandleStickGroup.md) for the full state machine, layout snapshot details, and token reference.

## Accessibility

The chart implements all reusable ARIA accessibility layers used across charts in this codebase.

### ChartAccessibility Wrapper

The chart is wrapped by `ChartAccessibility` with `chartType="candlestick"`, which provides:

- `role="figure"` container with `aria-label` derived from chart title
- `aria-describedby` linking to the auto-generated summary and hidden data table
- Auto-generated natural language summary (e.g. _"candlestick chart titled Stock Price. Shows 7 data points. Values range from 250 to 710."_)
- Visually-hidden `<table>` with Open, High, Low, Close columns for screen readers
- `aria-live="polite"` region for debounced hover/focus announcements

### OHLC-Aware Live Announcements

When a candle is hovered or focused, the `aria-live` region announces the full OHLC data:

> "23:00, Open 400, High 900, Low 200, Close 700"

The chart looks up the full data point by `hoverData.index` from the `data` array, so all four values are always available regardless of what the `CandleStickHoverData` callback carries.

### Keyboard Navigation

Each `CandleStick` within the group receives roving tabindex props via `useRovingTabIndex` for ArrowLeft/ArrowRight navigation. The group acts as a single tab stop.

### Per-Candle ARIA

Each candle gets a rich OHLC aria-label composed by the group:

> "23:00: Open 400, High 900, Low 200, Close 700, candle 1 of 7"

### aria-controls Link

When `dataDisplay={true}`, the stable `dataDisplayId` returned by `useChartAccessibility` links each interactive candle to the `DataDisplay` region via `aria-controls`, so screen readers can announce the associated data display.

### Element ARIA Summary

| Element       | ARIA                                                                     |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Chart wrapper | `role="figure"`, `aria-label`, `aria-describedby` (summary + data table) |
| Hidden table  | Visually hidden `<table>` with Category, Open, High, Low, Close columns  |
| CandleStick   | `role="button"`, OHLC `aria-label`, roving `tabIndex`, `aria-controls`   |
| Candle group  | `role="group"`, `aria-label="Chart data"`                                |
| YAxis         | `aria-hidden` (baked in)                                                 |
| XAxis         | `aria-hidden` (baked in)                                                 |
| AvgLine       | `aria-hidden="true"`                                                     |
| HoverBadge    | `aria-hidden` (baked in)                                                 |
| Live region   | `aria-live="polite"`, OHLC-aware debounced hover announcements           |

